WEBVTT

00:00:06.430 --> 00:00:08.140
What do you want from me...?

00:00:09.390 --> 00:00:11.130
Are you trying to tell me something?

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:17.740
These Numbers we retrieved from those ruins are trying to tell me something...

00:00:21.370 --> 00:00:22.700
<i>Long long ago...</i>

00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:25.080
<i>Hearing about the knights' rebellion, the Hero rushed back...</i>

00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:32.710
<i>...his beloved steed Pegasus stood in front of the knights, trying to protect his master.</i>

00:00:25.870 --> 00:00:32.710
<i>And then, the Hero, together with Pegasus' soul, was called to Heaven.</i>

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:34.920
<i>In this land, there was said...</i>

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:39.300
<i>But letting the prince lose in front of 
such a large crowd was not allowed.</i>

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:38.800
<i>The prince pleaded desperately for his rival, the gladiator,</i>

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:41.590
<i>...they wouldn't listen to him, and then, in front of a large crowd,</i>

00:00:41.590 --> 00:00:45.060
<i>the gladiator was cruelly executed.</i>

00:00:47.390 --> 00:00:51.750
<i>Those legends I saw just now... Could it be...?!</i>

00:00:55.750 --> 00:00:57.510
<i>Alit... You...</i>

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:02.360
<i>What in the world happened to you?
 Why'd you become like that?</i>

00:01:03.750 --> 00:01:04.230
Hey!

00:01:05.790 --> 00:01:07.170
What are you spacing out about?

00:01:07.650 --> 00:01:08.850
Uh, I'm not...

00:01:10.160 --> 00:01:13.790
You're probably stressing yourself thinking about that Barian guy named Alit.

00:01:14.170 --> 00:01:17.170
Y-Yeah, he just changed suddenly...

00:01:17.630 --> 00:01:18.520
Why would he now of all times?!

00:01:19.030 --> 00:01:21.750
He just showed his true face as a Barian.

00:01:22.630 --> 00:01:24.720
True face? But Alit...

00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:27.290
We will soon be arriving at Point 107.

00:01:27.570 --> 00:01:30.010
We will find the fourth set of ruins there.

00:01:30.390 --> 00:01:33.490
Wow! I wonder what kind of ruins we'll find next?

00:01:34.390 --> 00:01:38.030
I wonder if there's a legend at the ruins we'll go to next?

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:41.380
You could be right... It may be another sad tale...

00:01:42.350 --> 00:01:43.730
The legends of the ruins...

00:01:48.790 --> 00:01:50.890
<i>Galaxy-Eyes is resonating...?</i>

00:01:53.920 --> 00:01:55.610
<i>Could this possibly be...?</i>

00:02:06.570 --> 00:02:12.750
The legend I suddenly felt while retrieving the Number hidden away in those ruins...

00:02:13.810 --> 00:02:16.350
Why did I know that legend?

00:02:18.970 --> 00:02:19.590
Durbe.

00:02:20.790 --> 00:02:23.400
It seems you located another set of ruins with a Number.

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:28.230
Yeah. Unfortunately, though,
 Astral and the others took the Number.

00:02:29.490 --> 00:02:30.670
That doesn't sound like you.

00:02:31.350 --> 00:02:33.210
What's wrong? What happened?

00:02:33.770 --> 00:02:38.500
At the ruins with the Number, I somehow found myself assaulted by a mysterious sensation.

00:02:38.500 --> 00:02:39.010
What?

00:02:39.640 --> 00:02:41.770
There was a legend left behind at those ruins...

00:02:42.390 --> 00:02:45.800
The moment I made contact,
 something in my heart resonated with it.

00:02:46.710 --> 00:02:49.570
It was as if something called out to the memories inside me...

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:51.040
What do you mean?

00:02:51.750 --> 00:02:55.040
I do not know. But there are seven ruins with Numbers...

00:02:55.720 --> 00:02:57.400
And we are the Seven Emperors.

00:02:58.250 --> 00:02:59.850
Do you believe that to be a mere coincidence?

00:03:00.520 --> 00:03:01.560
What are you trying to say?

00:03:01.960 --> 00:03:07.110
Are you suggesting we have some relation
 to some foolish human legends?

00:03:07.850 --> 00:03:10.920
What nonsense! We need to focus on finding those Numbers in the ruins now!

00:03:11.480 --> 00:03:13.630
We can't let them outdo us any longer!

00:03:15.890 --> 00:03:16.720
Misael...

00:03:29.510 --> 00:03:31.850
Control unmanageable! Control unmanageable!

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:35.050
Yuma! Control your steering!

00:03:35.210 --> 00:03:36.690
I am!

00:03:38.030 --> 00:03:39.450
Wah! Why? Why?!

00:03:39.750 --> 00:03:43.360
Our equipment is being affected by something!

00:03:43.970 --> 00:03:46.950
Orbital! It doesn't matter where! Just land this ship somewhere!

00:03:47.770 --> 00:03:50.590
A-Affirmative!

00:04:18.170 --> 00:04:25.720
<i>Being best friends doesn't mean we always were</i>

00:04:25.720 --> 00:04:28.770
<i>That's pretty much true</i>

00:04:29.060 --> 00:04:36.230
<i>I found you during our serious battles</i>

00:04:36.400 --> 00:04:39.780
<i>The other me inside myself</i>

00:04:39.780 --> 00:04:44.660
<i>Awakening from within the conflict</i>

00:04:44.660 --> 00:04:51.000
<i>A turn for a chance! Seize it! Draw!</i>

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:54.210
<i>Duel! Dualism!</i>

00:04:54.210 --> 00:04:57.090
<i>These cards are polished to fit each other</i>

00:04:57.090 --> 00:05:01.720
<i>My fated opponent is my heart reflected through the mirror</i>

00:05:01.720 --> 00:05:04.800
<i>And if we end up with a "tie" in the end,</i>

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:13.270
<i>when we fall, all covered with mud, we'll praise each other</i>

00:05:27.890 --> 00:05:29.050
There is no mistake.

00:05:29.550 --> 00:05:34.020
The coordination points on the map inside the airship state the ruins are here.

00:05:36.140 --> 00:05:40.860
"The Trial For Galaxy-Eyes Users! Kaito's Do-Or-Die Duel"

00:05:37.020 --> 00:05:40.900
So the next ruins with the Number
 are on top of that rocky mountain?

00:05:41.690 --> 00:05:44.820
I guess we have no choice but to move on our own from here on.

00:05:44.820 --> 00:05:45.610
Eh?!

00:05:45.610 --> 00:05:47.150
That seems to be the case.

00:05:47.820 --> 00:05:49.870
Forgive me, Kaito-<i>sama</i>.

00:05:50.200 --> 00:05:52.830
My body isn't listening to what I tell it!

00:05:53.330 --> 00:05:57.160
I can't climb up that thing! I'm going to be left out again?!

00:05:58.370 --> 00:05:59.380
I guess so.

00:05:59.380 --> 00:06:02.340
They can't expect us girls to climb up that thing.

00:06:02.340 --> 00:06:03.090
Eh?

00:06:03.550 --> 00:06:06.590
Very well, Kotori-<i>san</i>. Let's stay here together.

00:06:07.380 --> 00:06:11.300
Oh, thank goodness! When you say it, Rio-<i>san</i>, I feel at ease!

00:06:11.680 --> 00:06:13.510
It will be my turn!

00:06:14.640 --> 00:06:17.890
Up we go! Then I'm off!

00:06:18.390 --> 00:06:20.100
Be careful, Yuma!

00:06:20.480 --> 00:06:23.900
I'll take care of it, Kotori!
 I'm the son of an adventurer!

00:06:23.900 --> 00:06:27.360
There you go saying that again!
 You shouldn't get too full of yourself!

00:06:28.030 --> 00:06:30.820
Listen, you... Don't go sounding like my sis!

00:06:30.820 --> 00:06:34.330
Get your butt back here as soon as you get the Number!

00:06:34.870 --> 00:06:36.200
Will do!

00:06:38.750 --> 00:06:39.580
Listen good!

00:06:40.290 --> 00:06:43.920
When mountain climbing,
 you have to first get a good foot holding...

00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:46.380
Then you reach out with your arms. Got it?!

00:06:47.210 --> 00:06:50.010
And it's really important that we help each other up the mountain.

00:06:50.380 --> 00:06:51.890
Going on your own is a no-no!

00:06:51.930 --> 00:06:55.680
Oh, shut up! I have no reason to take orders from you!

00:07:02.770 --> 00:07:04.110
Astral, what was that just now?!

00:07:04.610 --> 00:07:07.610
Most likely... the cry of a dragon...

00:07:10.780 --> 00:07:14.530
<i>Galaxy-Eyes...! As I thought, these ruins are...!</i>

00:07:26.590 --> 00:07:29.720
That's why I said we gotta help each other up the mountain!

00:07:32.640 --> 00:07:35.010
Do you think Yuma and the others will be all right?

00:07:35.640 --> 00:07:37.060
Kaito-<i>sama</i>!

00:07:37.220 --> 00:07:38.310
They'll be fine.

00:07:38.850 --> 00:07:39.890
If it's those three.

00:07:41.140 --> 00:07:43.400
That aside, would you care for a snack?

00:07:43.900 --> 00:07:44.980
Ahah!

00:07:44.980 --> 00:07:46.020
You're gonna get fat.

00:07:46.110 --> 00:07:47.360
Say that again, you hunk of junk!

00:07:56.990 --> 00:07:57.240
Huh?

00:07:59.290 --> 00:08:01.000
Th-This is the summit?

00:08:02.250 --> 00:08:03.580
I can't see anything through the fog...

00:08:05.210 --> 00:08:07.250
No, look carefully in front of you.

00:08:07.670 --> 00:08:07.880
Huh?

00:08:10.210 --> 00:08:12.090
Wh-What is that...?

00:08:16.220 --> 00:08:18.260
Are... Are you serious?!

00:08:20.270 --> 00:08:21.600
Something like this was at the top?

00:08:35.740 --> 00:08:38.450
A-Awesome!

00:08:40.540 --> 00:08:42.290
What's going on with this place?

00:08:42.870 --> 00:08:46.500
It may be another trap set by those Barian guys.

00:08:47.040 --> 00:08:47.750
Stay alert!

00:08:53.220 --> 00:08:53.800
That smell...

00:08:54.130 --> 00:08:55.510
H-Hey, Yuma!

00:08:56.050 --> 00:08:57.050
I definitely smell something...

00:08:57.600 --> 00:08:58.180
Is it a Barian?

00:08:59.470 --> 00:09:01.060
I smell something delicious!

00:09:09.940 --> 00:09:11.730
That looks yummy!

00:09:18.870 --> 00:09:21.200
You... damned fool!

00:09:23.660 --> 00:09:25.790
That hurt...! What's the big idea?!

00:09:26.120 --> 00:09:28.130
That would be my line!

00:09:28.380 --> 00:09:30.710
Stealing someone's meal without permission...!

00:09:31.500 --> 00:09:33.670
I was just gonna take a peek!

00:09:34.300 --> 00:09:36.970
No, you definitely said it looked yummy!

00:09:37.590 --> 00:09:38.890
No, you're wrong!

00:09:39.220 --> 00:09:39.930
You lie!

00:09:40.600 --> 00:09:41.810
I do not lie!

00:09:41.970 --> 00:09:44.770
You lie, lie, lie, lie, lie!

00:09:44.850 --> 00:09:45.390
Hmm?

00:09:46.640 --> 00:09:48.150
And who might you two be?

00:09:48.850 --> 00:09:52.530
My name is Kaito. We're here looking for the ruins containing the Number.

00:09:53.150 --> 00:09:55.320
Hmm? Number?

00:10:02.700 --> 00:10:04.500
Are you... a Dragon User?

00:10:05.080 --> 00:10:09.170
Yeah. And I also feel an unusual spirit coming from you.

00:10:17.550 --> 00:10:18.720
So you really are...!

00:10:19.640 --> 00:10:23.890
My name is Jinlong. I am the guardian of this Number.

00:10:24.520 --> 00:10:27.480
You have a pretty decent fighting spirit going for you.

00:10:28.980 --> 00:10:32.440
I know of a Duelist just like you!

00:10:32.480 --> 00:10:32.980
What?

00:10:33.360 --> 00:10:36.780
The legend left behind from these ruins says

00:10:36.780 --> 00:10:40.910
there was a Duelist who fought against dragons long ago.

00:10:41.490 --> 00:10:44.240
That Duelist was named Misael, right?

00:10:44.870 --> 00:10:45.370
What?!

00:10:45.660 --> 00:10:50.290
Oh? So you know of the legend surrounding these ruins?

00:10:50.750 --> 00:10:52.330
J-Just wait a minute!

00:10:52.750 --> 00:10:55.380
Why Misael? He's a Barian...

00:10:56.010 --> 00:11:00.010
The Numbers we retrieved from the ruins shared those memories with me.

00:11:01.590 --> 00:11:03.890
The seven Numbers we've been searching for...

00:11:04.810 --> 00:11:06.680
The legends surrounding these ruins

00:11:07.100 --> 00:11:10.730
are tales from when the Seven Barian Emperors were still human.

00:11:12.900 --> 00:11:15.730
Impossible! Those Barians used to be human?!

00:11:16.610 --> 00:11:17.530
That's correct.

00:11:19.030 --> 00:11:21.320
Then the legends of the ruins we've been to so far...

00:11:22.200 --> 00:11:24.450
...were Durbe's, Alit's, and Vector's...?

00:11:25.910 --> 00:11:27.160
Back from when they were human...?

00:11:27.540 --> 00:11:28.870
Yuma! Shark!

00:11:30.210 --> 00:11:32.290
Let me handle this Duel.

00:11:32.710 --> 00:11:33.750
K-Kaito!

00:11:34.290 --> 00:11:37.210
It isn't a mere coincidence that I found my way here.

00:11:37.630 --> 00:11:41.630
It was destiny... No, my fate as a Dragon User.

00:11:42.260 --> 00:11:43.180
Very well.

00:11:43.550 --> 00:11:48.560
If you manage to defeat me, I will hand over the Number from this ruin to you.

00:11:49.310 --> 00:11:53.060
But if you lose, I will be taking your Dragon!

00:11:53.480 --> 00:11:56.520
Fine by me, because I don't plan on losing.

00:11:56.940 --> 00:12:00.530
How long will that cheeky attitude work for you?!

00:12:00.740 --> 00:12:03.200
Duel mode! Photon Change!

00:12:16.210 --> 00:12:16.630
Duel!!

00:12:19.800 --> 00:12:21.420
Let me ask you something.

00:12:22.220 --> 00:12:25.640
Was it you who fought against Misael from the legend of these ruins?

00:12:26.350 --> 00:12:28.760
And did you defeat Misael?

00:12:29.100 --> 00:12:30.930
I wonder about that.

00:12:31.430 --> 00:12:33.140
My turn! Draw!

00:12:33.770 --> 00:12:38.070
I Summon Mythical Wood Dragon!

00:12:41.190 --> 00:12:44.240
When I control an Earth-Attribute Monster on the field,

00:12:44.360 --> 00:12:46.280
I can Special Summon this guy from my hand!

00:12:47.280 --> 00:12:51.330
Show yourself, Mythical Water Dragon!

00:12:52.870 --> 00:12:56.460
I then activate the effect of Mythical Wood Dragon!

00:12:56.790 --> 00:12:59.800
When I have a Water-Attribute Monster on my field,

00:13:00.130 --> 00:13:01.670
its level can be doubled!

00:13:02.260 --> 00:13:05.130
He got out two Level Eight Monsters in the blink of an eye!

00:13:05.510 --> 00:13:05.930
Here it comes!

00:13:07.970 --> 00:13:09.680
Now behold!

00:13:10.600 --> 00:13:14.850
I Overlay my Level Eight Mythical Wood Dragon and Mythical Water Dragon!

00:13:16.900 --> 00:13:20.940
I use these two Monsters to build the Overlay Network!

00:13:21.190 --> 00:13:22.530
Xyz Summon!

00:13:23.900 --> 00:13:27.280
Show yourself! Number 46!

00:13:30.910 --> 00:13:32.910
Your roar becomes thunder!

00:13:33.080 --> 00:13:35.000
You glisten like lightning!

00:13:35.830 --> 00:13:38.790
Manifest before us, my golden dragon!

00:13:39.380 --> 00:13:42.420
Ethereal Dragon - Draggluong!

00:13:46.840 --> 00:13:49.350
S-So that's the Number from these ruins?!

00:13:49.890 --> 00:13:52.640
Number 46, Draggluong...!

00:13:53.220 --> 00:13:54.890
So that's your Dragon, is it?

00:13:55.480 --> 00:13:58.190
That's right. It's the strongest Dragon.

00:13:58.350 --> 00:14:01.320
Interesting. Then show me that power!

00:14:01.570 --> 00:14:05.440
Very well! I will activate the effect of Draggluong!

00:14:05.740 --> 00:14:10.280
When I don't have a Dragon-Type Monster on my field other than this Monster,

00:14:10.490 --> 00:14:15.950
I can detach one Overlay Unit to Special Summon one Dragon from my hand!

00:14:16.460 --> 00:14:20.290
Come! Armed Divine Dragon - Protect Dragon!

00:14:24.670 --> 00:14:26.220
What?! The Number...!

00:14:26.920 --> 00:14:28.630
Draggluong disappeared!

00:14:30.220 --> 00:14:32.720
Time for Draggluong's Monster Effect!

00:14:33.060 --> 00:14:36.600
As long as I control another Dragon-Type Monster on my field,

00:14:36.930 --> 00:14:39.650
it cannot be targeted by attacks or effects!

00:14:39.770 --> 00:14:44.650
In other words, you won't be able to
 land a single finger on my Number!

00:14:45.360 --> 00:14:51.120
Then, I equip the Equip Magic, Dragon Shield, with Protect Dragon!

00:14:51.410 --> 00:14:55.870
The Dragon equipped with this card cannot be destroyed through battle nor effect,

00:14:56.160 --> 00:14:57.910
and casting off all Battle Damage!

00:14:58.660 --> 00:15:03.090
And when Protect Dragon is equipped with an Equip Magic,

00:15:03.250 --> 00:15:05.880
it raises its Attack Power by 500 points!

00:15:06.510 --> 00:15:10.470
Unless he can beat Protect Dragon, he can't defeat the Number!

00:15:10.470 --> 00:15:14.100
Unless he destroys that Equip Card, Kaito will...

00:15:14.140 --> 00:15:15.430
But that won't happen!

00:15:15.970 --> 00:15:19.230
I activate Protect Dragon's other effect!

00:15:19.770 --> 00:15:22.480
When this card is face-up on the field,

00:15:22.770 --> 00:15:27.860
Equip Magic Cards cannot be destroyed via Monster, Magic, or Trap effects!

00:15:28.610 --> 00:15:29.320
What did he say?!

00:15:29.530 --> 00:15:30.360
Th-Then...!

00:15:31.280 --> 00:15:34.240
Right. With Dragon Shield, Protect Dragon

00:15:34.410 --> 00:15:36.450
is a card that protects other effects.

00:15:37.290 --> 00:15:39.750
Now he can't destroy either,

00:15:39.870 --> 00:15:41.040
and it's become an impregnable shield.

00:15:42.750 --> 00:15:44.840
I end my turn with that!

00:15:46.800 --> 00:15:49.010
My turn! Draw!

00:15:51.880 --> 00:15:54.470
I Summon Overlay Sniper!

00:15:59.520 --> 00:16:02.520
Then I Special Summon Overlay Booster!

00:16:03.270 --> 00:16:08.820
When I have a Monster with 2000 or more Attack Points, this card can be Special Summoned!

00:16:09.690 --> 00:16:13.740
I release Overlay Sniper and Booster, both with 2000 or more Attack Points!

00:16:17.450 --> 00:16:19.120
The Galaxy that shines within the Darkness,

00:16:19.120 --> 00:16:22.500
Become the Light of Hope and obey me as my servant!

00:16:23.120 --> 00:16:25.460
The Incarnation of Light will now descend!

00:16:25.960 --> 00:16:29.210
Appear, Galaxy-Eyes Photon Dragon!

00:16:30.800 --> 00:16:32.130
Galaxy-Eyes!

00:16:32.800 --> 00:16:36.260
But how does Kaito plan to deal with Jinlong's Monsters?

00:16:36.800 --> 00:16:37.930
As expected, Kaito.

00:16:38.310 --> 00:16:40.970
Now he can break through his impregnable defense.

00:16:41.640 --> 00:16:43.020
Huh? What are you talking about?

00:16:43.600 --> 00:16:44.650
You forgot?!

00:16:46.150 --> 00:16:47.940
When Galaxy-Eyes battles,

00:16:48.400 --> 00:16:51.860
its effect Banishes itself and the attacking Monster.

00:16:53.820 --> 00:16:55.450
If he Banishes Protect Dragon,

00:16:55.910 --> 00:16:58.950
he'll lose Dragon Shield and it can be destroyed!

00:16:59.080 --> 00:17:02.700
It put you through a lot of pain and suffering!

00:17:02.700 --> 00:17:04.080
Th-That's right!

00:17:07.170 --> 00:17:09.880
So that's your Dragon, huh?

00:17:10.090 --> 00:17:14.130
Yeah! I plan to show you the power of my Dragon this time!

00:17:14.130 --> 00:17:15.720
I wonder about that.

00:17:16.390 --> 00:17:16.840
What?!

00:17:17.260 --> 00:17:20.890
At this moment, I activate Draggluong's other effect!

00:17:21.680 --> 00:17:26.270
It negates the effects of a 
Dragon-Type Monster on my opponent's field!

00:17:30.900 --> 00:17:31.820
Galaxy-Eyes!

00:17:32.400 --> 00:17:33.280
What now?!

00:17:35.200 --> 00:17:38.660
This is no different than your Dragon losing its fangs!

00:17:38.910 --> 00:17:40.620
So how do you plan to overcome this?!

00:17:41.410 --> 00:17:43.250
This impregnable wall?!

00:17:44.120 --> 00:17:44.710
Kaito!

00:17:45.960 --> 00:17:49.460
You may have wanted to see me suffer and lose all hope

00:17:49.460 --> 00:17:53.380
before your iron defense and impregnable wall...

00:17:54.420 --> 00:17:56.340
...but I'll break right through that iron defense!

00:17:56.880 --> 00:18:00.180
I activate the Quick-Play Magic, Book of Moon!

00:18:02.970 --> 00:18:06.350
This card targets one face-up Monster on the field,

00:18:06.350 --> 00:18:08.270
and switches it to Face-Down Defense Position!

00:18:10.480 --> 00:18:11.900
So there's that method, too...

00:18:12.520 --> 00:18:16.490
Equip Spells can't be equipped to Face-Down Monsters!

00:18:17.070 --> 00:18:20.410
That means the Dragon Shield
 is destroyed now that it's lost its target!

00:18:22.240 --> 00:18:24.620
Now I can see your Number again.

00:18:25.250 --> 00:18:28.750
Just you wait. I'll break through your iron wall
 with everything I've got!

00:18:29.250 --> 00:18:31.460
Then I'll beat your Number with my own hands!

00:18:32.090 --> 00:18:33.550
Go, Galaxy-Eyes!

00:18:33.960 --> 00:18:36.720
Attack the Protect Dragon that's been switched face-down!

00:18:37.380 --> 00:18:39.970
Photon Stream of Destruction!

00:18:47.600 --> 00:18:50.270
Whoa, he did it! A head start punch!

00:18:51.100 --> 00:18:53.400
Just what is this Duel...

00:18:54.650 --> 00:18:56.150
This is how I do things.

00:18:57.780 --> 00:18:59.610
There is no wall I can't break down.

00:18:59.860 --> 00:19:01.490
Now that's amusing!

00:19:04.490 --> 00:19:08.290
There is not a single opponent that cannot be destroyed.

00:19:08.290 --> 00:19:09.620
That was splendid!

00:19:09.920 --> 00:19:13.380
I give you a passing score.

00:19:13.790 --> 00:19:15.380
I don't like that.

00:19:15.380 --> 00:19:17.840
I don't need test scores from someone like you!

00:19:18.300 --> 00:19:19.550
It's meant as a compliment!

00:19:20.130 --> 00:19:24.050
I swear, there are so many Dragon User bigots in this world!

00:19:26.140 --> 00:19:28.770
Misael was the same!

00:19:29.020 --> 00:19:31.100
You remind me of him in so many ways!

00:19:31.600 --> 00:19:33.150
The way he Dueled...

00:19:33.730 --> 00:19:36.230
Don't be ridiculous! I'm nothing like him!

00:19:37.480 --> 00:19:40.400
Oh, really? So you say you're different from Misael?

00:19:41.030 --> 00:19:43.620
Man, I guess we'll put the pleasantries aside!

00:19:43.660 --> 00:19:48.660
Kaito, show me the full essence of your Dueling!

00:19:49.040 --> 00:19:52.670
There's still one last impregnable fortress
 you must breach, after all!

00:19:53.290 --> 00:19:56.340
In other words, I'll keep going until I've destroyed everything!

00:19:57.130 --> 00:19:59.720
I set one card face-down and end my turn!

00:20:03.680 --> 00:20:04.470
<i>So this is the place?</i>

00:20:06.260 --> 00:20:08.060
<i>These are the ruins containing the Number?</i>

00:20:13.850 --> 00:20:15.730
<i>That's the radiant spirit of a Dragon!</i>

00:20:20.900 --> 00:20:22.780
My turn! Draw!

00:20:24.240 --> 00:20:27.280
I activate the effect of Draggluong!

00:20:27.910 --> 00:20:32.500
When there is no other Dragon-Type Monster on the field other than this card,

00:20:32.660 --> 00:20:38.000
I can detach one Overlay Unit to Special Summon one Dragon from my hand!

00:20:39.170 --> 00:20:41.800
Show yourself, Soul-Eating Divine Dragon!

00:20:42.090 --> 00:20:43.720
Drain Dragon!

00:20:46.550 --> 00:20:49.100
Now that another Dragon has appeared on his field...!

00:20:49.390 --> 00:20:51.140
Tch, he'll use that effect again!

00:20:51.930 --> 00:20:55.770
Now you can't lay a hand on my Number.

00:20:56.190 --> 00:21:01.320
Also, my Drain Dragon's Attack Power increases by

00:21:01.440 --> 00:21:05.990
the amount of Life Points my opponent has!

00:21:06.870 --> 00:21:07.490
What did you say?!

00:21:09.120 --> 00:21:15.670
Your Life is 4000. Thus, Drain Dragon's
 Attack Power goes up 4000 points!

00:21:23.220 --> 00:21:24.760
It's got 8000 Attack Points!

00:21:27.220 --> 00:21:30.010
Then, when this Monster is destroyed,

00:21:30.350 --> 00:21:35.140
the opposing player takes damage equal to half its Attack Power!

00:21:35.520 --> 00:21:39.610
Wh-What did he say?! So that means, even if he destroys his Monster,

00:21:39.940 --> 00:21:41.400
he'll take 4000 points of damage!

00:21:41.940 --> 00:21:43.530
But it's got 8000 Attack Points!

00:21:43.990 --> 00:21:46.610
If he takes an attack like that now, Kaito will...

00:21:47.740 --> 00:21:50.160
He'll lose if he destroys that Monster.

00:21:50.620 --> 00:21:53.370
But as it is now, he can't even destroy it.

00:21:53.830 --> 00:21:58.250
Plus, it's difficult to figure out how to overcome such overwhelming Attack Power.

00:21:59.210 --> 00:22:02.250
You can call this a new trial for Kaito...

00:22:03.000 --> 00:22:05.010
So, Kaito, what will you do?

00:22:21.150 --> 00:22:23.650
<i>Is it the world that's boring?</i>

00:22:23.650 --> 00:22:26.190
<i>Or maybe you're the one who's not gettin' serious?</i>

00:22:26.190 --> 00:22:27.400
<i>Do you understand?</i>

00:22:27.400 --> 00:22:28.820
<i>Do I understand?</i>

00:22:29.030 --> 00:22:31.700
<i>Already got my answers</i>

00:22:31.740 --> 00:22:34.200
<i>Once you start movin', you ain't stoppin'</i>

00:22:34.200 --> 00:22:36.750
<i>I go on thinkin' even while losin'.</i>

00:22:36.750 --> 00:22:37.830
<i>Do you understand?</i>

00:22:37.830 --> 00:22:38.870
<i>I understand!</i>

00:22:38.870 --> 00:22:42.250
<i>Our formula for reversal's already gathered</i>

00:22:42.250 --> 00:22:44.590
<i>You afraid it ain't comin' true?</i>

00:22:44.590 --> 00:22:47.720
<i>I gotta 'least give it a try</i>

00:22:47.720 --> 00:22:49.930
<i>Ain't no problem if they say I'm borin'</i>

00:22:49.930 --> 00:22:52.930
<i>True failure's when we stop movin'</i>

00:22:53.100 --> 00:22:54.890
<i>Come on! Ga, ga, ga, guys & dolls</i>

00:22:54.890 --> 00:22:56.270
<i>Go, go, go, go my way</i>

00:22:56.270 --> 00:22:58.140
<i>Oh, oh, oh, over ray</i>

00:22:58.440 --> 00:23:02.440
<i>Door's always open for you</i>

00:23:02.610 --> 00:23:07.530
<i>Bring your power forth and go way, go way</i>

00:23:07.530 --> 00:23:08.780
<i>I understand!</i>

00:23:08.780 --> 00:23:12.780
<i>And tears are no way, no way</i>

00:23:13.280 --> 00:23:18.160
<i>With all my strength, pave way, go way</i>

00:23:18.160 --> 00:23:19.370
<i>I understand!</i>

00:23:19.370 --> 00:23:23.500
<i>Got all the courage here</i>

00:23:23.500 --> 00:23:25.670
<i>You ought to understand!</i>

00:23:25.670 --> 00:23:27.880
<i>Go way, go way</i>

00:23:40.350 --> 00:23:42.270
Kaito is in great danger of losing!

00:23:43.150 --> 00:23:44.480
The difficult trial of these ruins

00:23:44.860 --> 00:23:47.190
leaves Kaito with no means to break through his strategy.

00:23:47.610 --> 00:23:50.740
Then, a new powerful threat emerges.

00:23:51.110 --> 00:23:52.740
It's got 8000 Attack Points?!

00:23:52.860 --> 00:23:54.490
Now he can't move at all...!

00:23:54.740 --> 00:23:56.410
You'll erase the light of truth?!

00:23:56.490 --> 00:23:58.160
What's going on up the mountain?!

00:23:58.450 --> 00:23:59.910
You still have a trump card?!

00:24:00.660 --> 00:24:02.330
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ZeXal II!

00:24:02.670 --> 00:24:05.500
"The Legend of Misael! The Divine Dragon
 that Became a Number"

00:24:06.040 --> 00:24:08.340
Show him the power of Neo Galaxy!
